{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>For in booths.</b> For they made booths after they crossed the Sea of Reeds, and also in the wilderness of Sinai where they stayed nearly a year, and so is the custom of all camps. Now this appointed time too is a remembrance of the exodus from Egypt. And if a questioner asks why this commandment is in Tishrei, the answer is that the cloud of HaShem was over the camp by day and the sun did not strike them, and from the days of Tishrei they began making booths because of the cold."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:03.162767232Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}